// fuzz-shape: fn-argument
// fuzz-expect: assemble-fail
// A hole in a function-argument position. The arg is refined to one survivor
// (Positive rejects 0 and -1), so the medium fills `1` with no guess — the
// arg-position synthesis path works end to end. But the callee returns Float
// and main returns that Float, so the emitted WAT threads an f64 through the
// i32 `_start` boundary and wat2wasm rejects it
// (`type mismatch in call, expected [i32] but got [f64]`). The medium proved
// the fill and still emitted a non-assemblable program: a codegen gap the
// hole-fill loop surfaces, not a synthesis fault.

type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn to_sample(n: Positive) -> Float with Pure = if n > 0 { 0.5 } else { 0.0 }

fn main() = to_sample(??)
